    <div class="item">
      <div class="meta"><h3>12 V Power-Distribution Monitor</h3><span class="dates">2026.09 – present</span></div>
      <p class="sub">Open-hardware power monitoring — firmware + backend + web dashboard</p>
      <ul>
        <li>End-to-end power-monitoring system: custom open-source PCB, ESP32-C3 firmware (C/ESP-IDF) sampling an INA226 at 10 Hz over a custom 20-byte TCP wire protocol, with adaptive 10 Hz / 0.1 Hz sampling by viewer presence</li>
        <li><b>Dual-path overcurrent protection</b> (hardware ALERT-pin comparator + independent backend threshold) with per-event time/voltage/current/power logging</li>
        <li><b>Dual-slot OTA with automatic rollback</b> and a custom two-slot partition table — a bad update cannot brick a deployed device</li>
        <li>Python backend (FastAPI, async TCP ingest, SQLite persistence, WebSocket live broadcast) + web dashboard — <a class="ref" href="https://github.com/FibreCase/dynamic-power-monitor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/FibreCase/dynamic-power-monitor</a> · <a class="ref" href="https://oshwhub.com/fibrecase/project_mfgowtnz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">oshwhub.com/fibrecase/project_mfgowtnz</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="item">
      <div class="meta"><h3>Wind-Resource Assessment Toolkit</h3><span class="dates">2026.06</span></div>
      <p class="sub">Python pipeline for wind-farm siting — QC, Weibull fitting, shear &amp; roses</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Multi-stage automated QC on SODAR/LIDAR radar (40–200 m) and met-mast (2–80 m) wind data: range / correlation / trend / missing-value checks</li>
        <li>Weibull distribution fitting, power-law wind-shear and air-density estimation, wind-energy-density roses, and per-height data-availability statistics; unit-tested — <a class="ref" href="https://github.com/FibreCase/WindAssess" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/FibreCase/WindAssess</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

